# One unit's verdict once clang has compiled it: what every compile that
# judges a unit says, in the order a refusal is read (design.md §4.19,
# §1.12; panel 224; panel 245's R1, provisional, author ratification
# pending; defect 2464).
#
# A unit's own compile is not its only judge. **A unit holding the value
# region is read once more by the front end** under C's own meaning of a
# signed shift, its verdict counting only where every error it adds to the
# compile's is the region's (`cli/front_check.hero`, panel 224), and it is
# read whether the compile refused the unit or not, since its words are the
# truer ones. **Then the compile's own refusal.** **Then, where the unit
# holds a group's header region and was compiled above `-O0`, that region's
# code judged at `-O0`** (`cli/region_level.hero`), whose refusal is the
# unit's, so a program has one verdict at every level: under panel 245's R1
# every warning in a header's code is an error, and clang says a call to a
# function its header marks `warning` at `-O0` and not where `-O2` inlines
# it away, so `heroes build` refused what `heroes run` built (the sitting's
# `attr_warning` shape) until this compile.
#
# Each refusal is handed back as its reader made it, its code and its words;
# `cli/units.hero`'s `tu_object` appends the generated C's path and publishes
# nothing. Split out of that module at panel 245's landing, which took it
# past §11's 300 lines.

use cli/compiling
use cli/front_check
use cli/publish
use cli/region_level
use cli/toolchain

# The verdict of the unit at `c_file`, whose text is `tu_text`, compiled by
# `line` under `under` with `compiled` what clang answered: `ok` where every
# judge passes it, else the first refusal in the order above. `err_path` is
# the compile's stderr file, which the front end's read writes again and
# this discards.
function of(t: toolchain.Toolchain, under: compiling.Compiling, line: [str], c_file: str, tu_text: str, dir: str, err_path: str, compiled: str?) -> ()?
    if front_check.holds(tu_text)
        fronted = front_check.refused(
            line: line,
            c_file: c_file,
            tu_text: tu_text,
            err_path: err_path,
            compiled: text_of(compiled)
        )
        publish.discard(err_path)

        if fronted.is_err()
            return fronted

    if compiled.is_err()
        return fail(code: code_of(compiled), msg: text_of(compiled))
    zero = region_level.judged(t, tu_text: tu_text, c_file: c_file, dir: dir, under: under)

    if zero.is_err()
        return fail(code: code_of(zero), msg: text_of(zero))
    return ok()

# A run's refusal, its words and its code (`toolchain.asked_of_clang`), ""
# where it passed.
function text_of(failed: str?) -> str
    match failed
        .ok    => return ""
        .err e => return e.msg

function code_of(failed: str?) -> str
    match failed
        .ok    => return ""
        .err e => return e.code
